      "id": "check-page-0e790b9419",
      "url": "https://climatelaunchpad.org/application-form/",
      "page": "application",
      "excerpt": "ClimateLaunchpad – Applications are closed Facebook – Instagram – LinkedIn – YouTube About the competition Back Competition info Apply now Trainers FAQ About Us Participating countries Back Participating countries Become a national organiser Partners Back Our partner network Partner up Blog Competition Applications are closed Have a green business or idea you want to develop further? ClimateLaunchpad is the competition for you – but applications for this edition are now closed. Thank you to everyone who applied! Accepted participants get a 3-day boot camp, mentoring, and the chance to compete in National and Regional finals. Top performers win a trip to the Global Grand Final in Singapore. S tay tuned for ClimateLaunchpad 2027! Note: Applications for the 2026 edition are now closed. Thank you to everyone who applied this year. Please follow our social media channels and stay tuned for ClimateLaunchpad 2027! Check your deadline: Choose your country Angola Argentina Australia Austria Brazil Cape Verde Colombia Costa Rica Cyprus Ecuador Egypt El Salvador Estonia Fiji Finland France Germany Ghana Greece Guatemala India Indonesia Japan Kenya Madagascar Mexico Moldova Morocco Namibia Netherlands Nigeria Papua New Guinea Peru Philippines Portugal Sierra Leone Singapore South Africa South Korea Spain Switzerland Tanzania Türkiye Uganda United Kingdom United States Vanuatu Vietnam Your"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-da342721f5",
      "url": "https://climatelaunchpad.org/blog/press-release-global-green-business-ideas-competition-open-for-applications/",
      "page": "application",
      "excerpt": "ClimateLaunchpad – Press release: Global Green Business Ideas Competition open for applications Facebook – Instagram – LinkedIn – YouTube About the competition Back Competition info Apply now Trainers FAQ About Us Participating countries Back Participating countries Become a national organiser Partners Back Our partner network Partner up Blog (Success) stories Press release: Global Green Business Ideas Competition open for applications Wanted: Green business ideas to fix climate change Delft, The Netherlands, 1 March 2021 – Starting today, the seventh edition of global green business ideas competition ClimateLaunchpad opens for applications. The programme, supported by EIT Climate-KIC and TU Delft, helps aspiring entrepreneurs grow their cleantech ideas into global businesses. Think of innovations in adaptation, renewable energy, food and agriculture, water, transportation, industrial technology, or any other way to tackle climate change. The ClimateLaunchpad formula has proven time and time again to be the key to climate positive business success. The Dutch scale-up Felyx (2016 National Winner), recently announced a 24 million in investment to maintain their position as the Benelux market leader in electric shared scooters and to expand within Europe. The textile waste tracking and trading platform Reverse Resources (2015 Estonian National Winner) announced its role in the"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-26b81e8366",
      "url": "https://climatelaunchpad.org/blog/yes-were-back-applications-2018-now-open-in-35-countries/",
      "page": "application",
      "excerpt": "ClimateLaunchpad – Yes, we’re back. Applications 2018 now open in 35 countries Facebook – Instagram – LinkedIn – YouTube About the competition Back Competition info Apply now Trainers FAQ About Us Participating countries Back Participating countries Become a national organiser Partners Back Our partner network Partner up Blog (Success) stories Yes, we’re back. Applications 2018 now open in 35 countries Calling all green business ideas Let the games begin. We just kicked off the 2018 edition of our global green business ideas competition. We’re now open for applications in 35 countries. Last year’s record amount of 1,000 green ideas nicely sets the bar for this year. Do you have a green idea that deserves business success? Apply now. We’ll help you think, act and grow big. Or do you know people with a green business idea? Please forward them this newsletter. And also please share our messages on Facebook , Twitter and LinkedIn . What kinds of ideas are we looking for? We scout the globe for all kinds of ideas that help fix climate change. Whether it’s a mind shift in urban mobility, a revolution in the food chain, a breakthrough in energy production or a radical rethink of waste management. Even ideas that are still on the back of a napkin are welcome to join. Fixing climate change, one start-up at a time Don’t let him hear it, but secretly we nickname our commander in chief"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-6d4e95920c",
      "url": "https://climatelaunchpad.org/meet-our-trainers/",
      "page": "application",
      "excerpt": "ClimateLaunchpad – Trainers Facebook – Instagram – LinkedIn – YouTube About the competition Back Competition info Apply now Trainers FAQ About Us Participating countries Back Participating countries Become a national organiser Partners Back Our partner network Partner up Blog Competition Meet our trainers for 2026! Our global network of expert green tech trainers sits at the heart of our program, bringing real-world venture experience to every boot camp and shaping the success of our participants and alumni. Certified Trainers Nirmala (Mala) Sukumar Mala K is a trainer, mentor, and program director with extensive experience leading regional initiatives in entrepreneurship, leadership development, employability, and workforce transformation. She has worked with organizations including UNESCO, Microsoft, Google.org, AVPN, PERKESO, Yayasan Petronas, Micron Foundation, IKEA SE, and the U.S. Embassy to design and deliver programs focused on youth empowerment, digital inclusion, entrepreneurial mindset development, and future-ready workforce ecosystems across Asia and beyond. Over the years, Mala has trained and mentored more than 1,200 entrepreneurs and youths in digital upskilling, business and social enterprise development, career readiness, and innovationdriven growth. She is also a mentor and coach under Hellomonday, supporting professionals, founders, and career pivoters"
    },
